<section image-layout="blank" id="rgYe7pz2V3" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="c5ebnafYzH"><h2>A good chart marks its limits</h2><p font-size="18pt"><b>The model charts evolution, not every origin question.</b> Honest navigators separate the evidence-supported route from what remains beyond the chart.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="ADjs_arDBY" border="2.6666666666666665px dashed palette-5" colspan="18"><labels><label variant="outline">Boundary marked</label></labels><h3>Before the earliest described phase</h3><p font-size="17pt">What preceded it remains uncertain. The model supplies no known launch point, outer void, or certain first cause.</p><p><b>The limit is part of the chart.</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="xStgClGF_n" background-color="surface" colspan="42"><labels><label variant="solid">Evidence-supported route</label></labels><h3>Development of the observable universe</h3><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="c2BN5a6hlO" colspan="15"><h4>Hot, dense phase</h4><p font-size="16pt">The model begins with early conditions.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="PiX6Ma_hTH" colspan="15"><h4>Nuclei</h4><p font-size="16pt">Cooling allows light nuclei to persist.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="03FwafCcaE" colspan="15"><h4>Atoms + free light</h4><p font-size="16pt">At about 380,000 years.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="o5Vgx67VBB" colspan="15"><h4>Stars + galaxies</h4><p font-size="16pt">Structure develops later.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="16pt"><b>No privileged center or navigable edge is required.</b></p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Source: <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/universe/overview/">NASA · Universe Overview</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>